### Demo 1 — local SQL Server
### VS Code REST Client, or copy the URLs into a browser.
@host = http://localhost:5000

### health — always the first call in any environment
GET {{host}}/health

### everything
GET {{host}}/api/policies

### filter, sort, page  (OData-like operators, parameterised under the hood)
GET {{host}}/api/policies?$filter=status eq 'active'&$orderby=premium desc&$first=5

### projection
GET {{host}}/api/policies?$select=policy_number,product,premium

### by primary key
GET {{host}}/api/policies/id/1

### the view
GET {{host}}/api/policy-summary?$filter=days_to_expiry lt 400

### insert
POST {{host}}/api/policies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policy_number": "POL-2026-0099",
  "product": "Motor - comprehensive",
  "status": "pending",
  "premium": 999.00,
  "commission_amount": 99.90,
  "broker_id": 1,
  "effective_date": "2026-09-01",
  "expiry_date": "2027-08-31"
}

### keyless PATCH — new in 2.0 when the database generates every omitted key
PATCH {{host}}/api/policies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policy_number": "POL-2026-0100",
  "product": "Travel - annual",
  "status": "active",
  "premium": 240.00,
  "commission_amount": 24.00,
  "broker_id": 2,
  "effective_date": "2026-09-01",
  "expiry_date": "2027-08-31"
}

### the stored procedure
POST {{host}}/api/renew-policy
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "policy_number": "POL-2026-0003",
  "months": 12
}

### OpenAPI document (Swagger UI lives at the same path in a browser)
GET {{host}}/api/openapi

### GraphQL — nested read through the declared relationship
POST {{host}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query { policies(filter: { status: { eq: \"active\" } }, orderBy: { premium: DESC }, first: 5) { items { policy_number product premium broker { name city } } } }"
}

### GraphQL — aggregation (SQL family only)
POST {{host}}/graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "query { policies { groupBy { fields { status } aggregations { sum(field: premium) count(field: id) } } } }"
}
